      },
      "lineNbr": 356,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T06:43:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What should happen if multiple entities register an OffloadCallback for the same interface? Given the current API shape is fine - we just send onOffloadUpdated to all of them.\n\nBut if we add transmit support down the line (which I think we\u0027re planning to do), then probably we can\u0027t allow multiple entities to register for the same interface? Because if we did, we\u0027d potentially get multiple responses for the same query?",
      "revId": "e9d86080b5d30d6f31cb4a717a7d60a52f902f61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9d8fe35_73a50c16",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 371,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T06:43:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we can do this check here. NsdManager is in app space. So two NsdManagers in different processes could both attempt to register for interface 42, and this check would not fail because they\u0027re in different processes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 371,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 371,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "e9d86080b5d30d6f31cb4a717a7d60a52f902f61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
