      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T06:43:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Info\" is a very generic word. We use it a lot because sometimes it\u0027s difficult to find a better choice, but it\u0027s worth trying to see if we can find some other option. OffloadedRecord? OffloadedService? ServiceOffload? ...? Or maybe OffloadedName? After all, service names and hostnames are both names...\n\nGiving it a name other than \"info\" (e.g., \"record\") might also make it clearer to users and readers of this code what the object represents and what it should do.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "e9d86080b5d30d6f31cb4a717a7d60a52f902f61",
